dzn: Copy partial depth-stencil regions, and honour bufferImageHeight

Direct3D 12 copies a depth-stencil resource only as a whole subresource.
A vkCmdCopyImage, vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer or vkCmdCopyBufferToImage that
covered part of a depth or stencil plane made the command list fail to
close, and vkEndCommandBuffer returned VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY. Image
copies now take the blit fallback; buffer copies go through a temporary
buffer holding the whole plane.

A placed footprint puts the slices of a 3D copy RowPitch * Height apart,
with Height the image extent's, so with a larger bufferImageHeight every
slice after the first went to the wrong place. Such regions take the
line-by-line copy. (The layer stride already used bufferImageHeight.)

From Oliver Bestmann's commits fa14a7a, e880d34, 04a4308 and 6cc1092 in
github.com/weaselway/mesa (MIT), where the dEQP-VK.api.copy_and_blit
depth-stencil, image_to_buffer and buffer_to_image groups and
image.concurrent_copy pass.

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
index 743483d..beeaa18 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
